Was KNOWNBUG since round 152 (main() partially type-checked; the converting
constructor found no match).  Fixed 2026-09-23 by the round-158 part-4
series: pack expansion in braced-init-lists and folds over type packs,
constant evaluation of __find_uniq_type_in_pack (loops, local arrays,
queued definitions), static data member templates (__exactly_once,
__accepted_index), using-declarator pack expansion (_Build_FUNs), the
member alias __to_type's default argument, variable template-id arguments
resolved at the point of use, and the type-for-non-type kind mismatch of
std::get<T> vs std::get<N> as a candidate removal.
